course: dictionary
lesson: 15013
title: Resolute: staying firm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Resolute is an adjective. It describes someone who has made up their mind and will not give up, even when things get hard. Read the clues around it. «The resolute girl practised her piano every day, even when her fingers ached.» Her fingers ached, but she kept going, so resolute means firm and determined.
explain: Resolute can also describe a look or a face. «He gave a resolute stare at the steep hill.» A stare that shows you won't back down is a resolute stare. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "firmly decided" fits, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Resolute is similar to determined, firm and steadfast, but it often sounds strong and calm. A resolute leader stands firm in hard times. A resolute effort means you keep trying, even when you feel like stopping.
fact: Resolute is an adjective, and it means firmly decided and not giving up.
fact: «Resolute» can also show determination, as in «a resolute look».
fact: Similar words for resolute are determined, firm and steadfast.
fact: «Resolute» is the opposite of giving up easily; a resolute person keeps going.
fact: In «Badger is resolute that Toad must change his ways», Badger has made up his mind and will not change it.
exercise: «The resolute girl practised her piano every day, even when her fingers ached.» What does resolute mean? | Quick to laugh at jokes | Very sleepy and tired | *Firmly decided and not giving up
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to resolute? | *Determined | Late | Lost | Silly
exercise: «Badger is resolute that Toad must change his ways.» What does this show? | Badger is bored and wants to leave | Badger is hungry | *Badger will not give up on his plan
test: «The resolute runner did not stop, even when her legs ached.» What does resolute show about her? | *Determination to keep going | She is sleepy and wants to rest | She is cold and wet
test: Which sentence uses resolute correctly? | «The resolute cake was eaten quickly.» | «The resolute leader stood firm when the storm came.» | *«The resolute captain would not let the ship turn back.» | «The resolute sun set behind the hill.»
exam: Ella was resolute about saving her money, so she never bought sweets. Which word is closest in meaning to resolute? | *Steadfast | Careless | Silly | Lazy
